-- non-conforming mappings are refused
SELECT kb.check_mapping('bad', $$
@prefix rr: <http://www.w3.org/ns/r2rml#> .
<#T> rr:logicalTable [ rr:tableName "hr.emp" ] ;
  rr:subjectMap [ rr:template "http://example.com/{id}" ; rr:class <Employee> ] .
$$);
ERROR:  non-conforming R2RML mapping: <Employee>, the object of its <http://www.w3.org/ns/r2rml#class>, is a relative IRI, and the mapping has no base IRI to resolve it against: give it one, as kb.add_mapping()'s base_iri or as an @base
CONTEXT:  R2RML mapping "bad"
SELECT kb.check_mapping('bad', $$
@prefix rr: <http://www.w3.org/ns/r2rml#> .
<#T> rr:logicalTable [ rr:tableName "hr.emp" ] ;
  rr:subjectMap [ rr:template "http://example.com/{nosuchcolumn}" ] .
$$);
